\nRental price starting from\n\nRM 1,800\n\nFor Sale (0)\n\n## Common facilities\n\nImage: security-access-control-o24-hour security  | Image: bbq-oBBQ\nImage: gym-oGym  | Image: parking-oParking\nImage: playground-oPlayground  | Image: yoga-oYoga Room\n\n## Building details\n\nBuilding  | # Floors  | # Units\n--- | --- | ---\nD'Sara Sentral, Sungai Buloh  | 504  | 247\n\n## Customer reviews\n\n5.0 out of 5\n\nBased on 7 reviews\n\nWrite a Review\n\n(328 Reviews)\n\n22 September 2025\n\nInvestor\n\nI rented here for 14 months. Units are well maintained, management is responsive, and being able to walk to the MRT was a huge draw for my tenants. Facilities aren’t super high-end compared to Mont Kiara condos, but they’re practical and clean. Biggest drawback is it’s leasehold, so for long-term buyers that might matter. For rental though, it’s been easy to attract tenants.\n\n(328 Reviews)\n\n22 September 2025\n\nFamily Perspective\n\nWe’ve been here with our two kids for over a year. The place feels safe, security guards are attentive, and the pool and gym are decent enough for daily use. Having shops and eateries downstairs makes life convenient, but sometimes the retail area brings more people around, so it can feel crowded. Still, overall it’s a comfortable home for a small family.\n\n(328 Reviews)\n\n22 September 2025\n\nCommuter Resident\n\nLiving at D’Sara Sentral has been a lifesaver for me because of the sky bridge straight to the MRT. I work in KL and don’t need to drive every day, which cuts down so much stress. The unit is modern and easy to maintain. The only thing is, for Sungai Buloh the price is on the higher side, but I guess you’re really paying for the connectivity.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nService Residence for Rent in D'sara Sentral by Steve Chen (https://www.iproperty.com.my/property/sungai-buloh/dsara-sentral/rent-501312046/)\nciteturn149search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago;